From 6744429808569a78479aa584539545d5c7e9ecac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 05:47:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Bluetooth: hci_conn: hold a reused SCO connection for its
 caller

hci_connect_sco() returns the connection with a hold that its caller
owns, and sco_connect() drops that hold when it is done with it. A new
connection gets the hold from hci_conn_link().

Since commit 06149746e720 ("Bluetooth: hci_conn: Add support for
linking multiple hcon"), a connection whose link already exists is
returned without one, and the ACL hold that hci_connect_acl() took for
the link is kept instead.

Since commit 8a5b0135d4a5 ("Bluetooth: SCO: fix race conditions in
sco_sock_connect()"), sco_connect() drops the hold when sco_chan_add()
fails, so a second connect() to a device whose SCO link is up drops
the hold of the socket that owns the link: sco_chan_add() fails with
EBUSY, hci_conn_timeout() then finds no holder, and the first socket's
link is disconnected.

Take a hold for the caller when the link exists, and drop the ACL
hold, which the existing link already owns, as commit e06d549fcd4a
("Bluetooth: hci_conn: fix CIS hold ownership on reuse") did for CIS.
The second connect() still fails with EBUSY; the first link is no
longer disconnected.

Fixes: 8a5b0135d4a5 ("Bluetooth: SCO: fix race conditions in sco_sock_connect()")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org # 6.6.x
Signed-off-by: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
---
 net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c | 17 +++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c b/net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c
index 29da3fe2b9538..603ddb7fe3d0d 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c
@@ -1911,11 +1911,20 @@ struct hci_conn *hci_connect_sco(struct hci_dev *hdev, int type, bdaddr_t *dst,
 		}
 	}
 
-	link = hci_conn_link(acl, sco);
-	if (!link) {
+	if (sco->link) {
+		/* The existing link already owns the hold on the ACL, and the
+		 * caller needs its own hold on the SCO connection, which
+		 * hci_conn_link() only takes for a new link.
+		 */
 		hci_conn_drop(acl);
-		hci_conn_drop(sco);
-		return ERR_PTR(-ENOLINK);
+		hci_conn_hold(sco);
+	} else {
+		link = hci_conn_link(acl, sco);
+		if (!link) {
+			hci_conn_drop(acl);
+			hci_conn_drop(sco);
+			return ERR_PTR(-ENOLINK);
+		}
 	}
 
 	sco->setting = setting;
-- 
